# Currently:

Edit /usr/share/X11/xkb/symbols/se directly.

Custom programming mappings are defined in programmer file.
Keep this file up to date with new mappings.
This file is not read by any program.
Copy/paste contents to the symbols/se file to the xkb_symbols "programmer" block.

Also, before: include "se(programmer)" within the xkb_symbols "basic" block.

Logging in and out seems neccessary.

# ##############################
# BELOW MIGHT BE TOO COMPLICATED
# ##############################

# I also suspect this is done automatically
# somehow, somewhere

# Custom mappings in ~/.xkb/symbols/programmer

# Base the layout upon 'se'
setxkbmap se

# Generate xkb file
setxkbmap -print > programmer.xkb

# Append symbols to base layout
Append '+programmer(basic)' to xkb_symbols line

# Load the xkb file
xkbcomp -I$HOME/.xkb ~/.xkb/programmer.xkb $DISPLAY

# Autoload: add the following lines to ~/.xprofile
if [ -n "$DISPLAY" ] && command -v xkbcomp >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    xkbcomp -I$HOME/.xkb ~/.xkb/programmer.xkb "$DISPLAY"
fi
